<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armando Diaz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1861–1928</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Armando Diaz was an Italian general who became chief of staff of the army in November 1917, after the defeat at Caporetto. He rebuilt morale, held the line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piave">Piave</a> in 1918 and directed the victory of Vittorio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veneto">Veneto</a> that ended the war on the Italian front. He was made a marshal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s first minister of war from 1922 to 1924.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armando-diaz.jpg" alt="Armando Diaz" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mario Nunes Vais · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armando_Diaz_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
